// Territory name -> ISO 3166-1 numeric, the join key for the world atlas.
//
// `world-atlas` keys its features by numeric id and carries only a Natural Earth
// display name ("W. Sahara", "Dem. Rep. Congo"), so matching on names at runtime
// would be guesswork against a moving target. The table is explicit instead.
//
// 159 of these were generated by normalising both sides (accent-fold, drop
// parentheticals, Rep. -> Republic); the seven that needed a human are marked
// below. `upande_crm/tests/test_territory.py` asserts every Territory on the
// site is either in this table or in MICRO_CENTROIDS, so a territory added
// later fails a test rather than vanishing off the map.
