// The seven above that no normalisation could reach, recorded so the next
// person does not try to "fix" them: Bosnia and Herzegovina (070), Democratic
// Republic of the Congo (180), Republic of the Congo (178), Equatorial Guinea
// (226), North Macedonia (807), Palestine State (275), South Sudan (728).

// Territories with no polygon at 110m resolution: micro-states and island
// nations. They render as centroid dots, which is not a fallback but the better
// answer — a two-pixel Singapore polygon is unhittable at any zoom, and the 50m
// atlas costs 650KB more without fixing that. [lon, lat].
